# Custom UI Components

If Chakra UI does not provide a ready-made component, build the component from Chakra primitives.

Use Chakra primitives as the base for custom UI:

- Box
- Flex
- Grid
- Stack
- HStack
- VStack
- Text
- Heading
- Icon
- Button
- Input
- FormControl

Do not introduce another styling system.

## Allowed

Use Chakra style props and theme tokens:

```tsx
<Box
  p="4"
  borderRadius="xl"
  bg="surface.primary"
  color="text.primary"
/>
```

## Forbidden

Do not use inline style attributes:

```tsx
<div style={{ padding: 16 }} />
```

Do not use styled-components:

```tsx
const Card = styled.div`
  padding: 16px;
`;
```

Do not create CSS files for component styling:

```tsx
import './card.css';
```

## Rules

- Use Chakra UI components first.
- Use Chakra primitives when a ready-made component does not exist.
- Use Chakra style props for layout, spacing, colors, typography, borders, shadows, and responsive styles.
- Use theme tokens instead of hardcoded values.
- Keep custom components small and focused.
- Do not create reusable shared UI components before the same pattern appears at least twice.
- Do not duplicate Chakra components with custom wrappers unless there is a real repeated use case.
